! Floating-point diagnostic jb_af1c, routine F210 "STORE ROUNDED TEST
! ROUTINE", sub-test A8 -- "TEST NORMALIZATION PROCESS"
! (docs/jb_af1c_floating-point.pdf p.111, octal 016054.40-016062.00,
! the routine's own exit "BD,$+1.0"). Eight rows, and it closes F210A.
!
! The first UNFLAGGED SRD(N): the one sub-test in the whole routine
! where SRD actually normalizes. A6 and A7 were SRD(N) too, but in the
! XFP/XFN ranges where normalization is suppressed, so the shift never
! ran. Here it runs, and it runs eleven places:
!
!   FK47 is exponent +50, fraction 000fffffffff -- eleven leading
!   zeros. C0011 drops FK22's all-ones fraction into the low half, so
!   the 96-bit fraction is 000fffffffff_ffffffffffff.
!   SRD(N) rounds: the +1 at IBM 60 carries out of the low half and
!   the kept 48 bits become 001000000000, with no overflow.
!   Normalizing that shifts left ELEVEN places to 800000000000 and
!   takes the exponent from +50 to +39.
!
!   Expected FK52 = exponent +39, fraction 800000000000.
!
! So A8 pins three things nothing before it touches: that the shift
! happens at all on the unflagged path, that its distance is counted
! from the ROUNDED sum rather than the original fraction (the original
! has eleven leading zeros only after the rounding carry lands), and
! that the exponent is adjusted by the shift.
!
! The manual adds "Low-order zeros are always supplied in the case of
! the left shift. Noisy mode does not affect this operation" (p.96) --
! the reason the model normalizes with noisy False whatever NM says.
! A8 cannot check that clause, though: its shifted-in bits are all
! zero either way here, because the rounded sum ends in zeros.
!
! ROS (022355) is the routine's scratch word, not a pool constant.
! Framework substitutes as everywhere else in this series: SERS (octal
! 1304) -> FAIL halt, SEN (octal 1310) -> scratch. Constants from the
! pool p.178. PASS sits at 016062.00, on the routine's exit; the four
! rows after it (BD,$+1.0 / B,FSR1 / SIC,SENO+.32 / B,SSW) are the
! SSIP return and are not transcribed. F210B "TEST UNCHANGED
! REGISTERS" begins at 016064.00 with label FSR2.
!
! Instructions: B, DL(U), C0011, SRD(N), L, CT0110, SIC, BRGZ.
! verify_fp_arith_f210a8_listing.py checks every word bit-for-bit.
!
! Observed: passed on the first run, with the pre-computed arithmetic
! matching FK52 exactly. An injection confirms it is the sole guard
! for SRD's unflagged normalization: forcing fpNormalize96Wide's mode
! to False -- so the unflagged path never shifts, whatever (N) says --
! halts A8 with SIC storing 016062.00, right after its BRGZ, while
! F210A1-A2, F210A3-A4, F210A5 and F210A6-A7 all stay green.
!
! That A6-A7 survives it is the point: they are SRD(N) too, but
! flagged, so their normalization was already suppressed and turning
! it off changes nothing. A8 is the only sub-test in F210 where the
! shift actually runs.

! -- SSIP framework substitutes --
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- the routine's scratch word --
        SLC, (8)22355.0
ROS     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- constants (pool p.178) --
        SLC, (8)022170.0
FK22    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0400177777777777777760
        SLC, (8)022221.0
FK47    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0031000017777777777760
        SLC, (8)022226.0
FK52    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0023500000000000000000

! The listing prints no label at 016054.40 -- ENTRY is ours, needed
! only as the END operand.
! -- code (verbatim, at the listing's addresses) --
        SLC, (8)16054.40
ENTRY   B, $+.32                               ! F210A8: test normalization process
        DL(U), FK47
        C0011(BU,48), FK22+.12, 20
        SRD(N), ROS
        L(BU), FK52
        CT0110(BU,60), ROS, 4                  ! test result exponent and fraction
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
PASS    BEW, $                                 ! 016062.00: the routine's exit ("BD,$+1.0")
        END, ENTRY
